.\" Man page for cargo-project
.\" Generated for version 0.1.0
.\" View with: man ./docs/man/cargo-project.1
.TH CARGO\-PROJECT 1 "2026" "0.1.0" "User Commands"
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH NAME
cargo\-project \- keeps your Rust workspace clean, fast, and push\-ready
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cargo project
.RI < noun >
.RI [ verb ]
.RI [ options ]

.B cargo\-project
.RI < noun >
.RI [ verb ]
.RI [ options ]
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cargo\-project
is a Rust workspace health and CI/CD helper.
It inspects git state, the active toolchain, Cargo workspace membership, and
more — then reports the overall workspace health through a composable
.IR noun-verb
command grammar.

All read\-only commands exit 0 on success.
Destructive commands require an explicit
.B \-\-confirm
flag so accidental invocations are always safe.

The tool can be invoked in two equivalent ways:

.RS 4
.nf
cargo project <noun> [verb] [options]   # as a cargo subcommand
cargo\-project <noun> [verb] [options]  # direct binary invocation
.fi
.RE

When a noun is given without a verb,
.B cargo\-project
injects a sensible default verb automatically — see
.B DEFAULT VERBS
below.
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH COMMANDS
.\" ── status ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS "status \- workspace health snapshot"
.TP
.B cargo project status
Short form.
Equivalent to
.B cargo project status show\fR.
.TP
.B cargo project status show [\-\-json] [\-\-verbose]
Display a one\-screen workspace health summary including:
git branch, dirty/staged/untracked file counts, and the active Rust toolchain.

.RS 4
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine\-readable JSON instead of the human\-friendly table.
Useful in CI pipelines and scripts.

.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
Print per\-file details for every dirty and staged file.
.RE
.\" ── workspace ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS "workspace \- workspace\-wide diagnostics"
.TP
.B cargo project workspace
Short form.
Equivalent to
.B cargo project workspace doctor\fR.
.TP
.B cargo project workspace doctor [\-\-json]
Run all workspace diagnostics:

.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Cargo.toml is present and well\-formed.
.IP \(bu 2
All workspace members resolve without errors.
.IP \(bu 2
.B rust\-toolchain.toml
(if present) matches the active toolchain.
.IP \(bu 2
No duplicate package names across workspace members.
.RE

.RS 4
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the diagnostic result as JSON.
.RE
.\" ── completions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS "completions \- shell completion script generator"
.TP
.B cargo project completions \-\-shell \fI<shell>\fR
Generate a tab\-completion script for
.I <shell>
and write it to stdout.
Redirect the output to the appropriate location for your shell (see
.B EXAMPLES
below).

Accepted values for
.IR <shell> :
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
.BR fish ,
.BR powershell ,
.BR elvish .
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH DEFAULT VERBS
When a bare noun is given without an explicit verb,
.B cargo\-project
automatically injects the default verb listed below:

.TS
tab(|) allbox;
l l.
Noun|Default verb
status|show
workspace|doctor
.TE

This means
.B cargo project status
and
.B cargo project status show
are identical.
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH OPTIONS
These options are accepted by the top\-level binary before any noun:

.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version number and exit.

.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help information.
Pass
.B \-\-help
after a noun or verb to see its specific options.
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
For
.B status show
this means the workspace is healthy (PASS or WARN).

.TP
.B 1
An error occurred, or the workspace is unhealthy (FAIL).

.TP
.B 2
Bad command\-line arguments (clap error).
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Controls the structured\-logging filter.
Set to
.B debug
to enable trace\-level adapter diagnostics:

.RS 4
.nf
RUST_LOG=debug cargo project status show
.fi
.RE

Default level:
.BR warn .

.TP
.B APP_ENV
Set to
.B ci
to switch to CI\-friendly output: colour is disabled, output is plain text
suitable for log aggregators.
Automatically implied when stdout is not a TTY.

.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to any non\-empty value, all ANSI colour sequences are suppressed
(per the
.UR https://no-color.org
No Color
.UE
specification).

.TP
.B CARGO_TERM_COLOR
Standard Cargo colour control.
Set to
.B never
to suppress colour in Cargo output that
.B cargo\-project
may invoke.
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH FILES
.TP
.I Cargo.toml
Workspace manifest read by all adapters.
Must be present in the working directory or a parent directory.

.TP
.I rust\-toolchain.toml
Optional toolchain pin.
Read by the toolchain adapter to verify the active Rust version.

.TP
.I cicd.toml
Optional state carrier written by
.B cargo\-project
after commands that mutate workspace state.
Human\-readable TOML; do not edit manually (changes are overwritten on the
next run).
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cargo project status
Show the workspace health snapshot.

.TP
.B cargo project status show \-\-json
Emit the snapshot as JSON (useful in CI):

.RS 4
.nf
{
  "workspace": "my\-crate",
  "git_phase": { "branch": "main", "dirty_files": 0, ... },
  "verdict": "PASS"
}
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B cargo project status show \-\-verbose
List every dirty/staged file below the summary line.

.TP
.B cargo project workspace doctor
Run all workspace diagnostics interactively.

.TP
.B cargo project completions \-\-shell bash > ~/.bash_completion.d/cargo\-project
Install bash tab\-completions for the current user.

.TP
.B cargo project completions \-\-shell zsh > ~/.zsh/completions/_cargo\-project
Install zsh tab\-completions (directory must be in
.IR $fpath ).

.TP
.B cargo project completions \-\-shell fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/cargo\-project.fish
Install fish tab\-completions (picked up automatically by fish).

.TP
.B ./scripts/install-completions.sh
Auto\-detect the current shell and install completions in the right place
without any manual redirects.
